=== compopt changes a spec's options
compopt +o bashdefault +o default +o dirnames -o filenames +o noquote +o nosort -o nospace +o plusdirs foo
complete -o nospace -W 'w' foo
=== Tab: word lists, prefixes, suffixes and filters
[svc stop ][]
[svc sta][]
[cfg key=][]
[wrap <one> ][]
=== Tab: directory and file actions, -X, -G
[mycd cdir/sub/][]
[view cdir/file.txt ][]
[cc1 cdir/file.c ][]
=== Tab: -F with compopt, -C, and COMPREPLY taken as it is
[opts chosen=][]
[anyc zz ][]
[cmdc beta ][]
=== Tab: a spec with no matches does not fall back to file names
[none cdir/fi][]
[fallback cdir/file.][]
=== Tab: -D for commands without a spec, loading one on 124
[newcmd loaded ][]
complete -W 'loaded' newcmd
=== Tab: -E on an empty line, -I for the command word
[empty-line ][]
[initial-word ][]
=== a spec is found by the command's last path component
[./svc stop ][]
=== a pipeline stage sees the specs
complete -W 'start stop status' svc
